# Python
venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# Node
node_modules/

# Pipeline scratch output (regenerable; never the source of truth)
work/

# FIFA PMSR source PDFs: copyrighted, ~570MB, and regenerable via
# download_pmsr_corpus.py. Never redistribute in a public repo (see brief
# risk note: displaying data with attribution is safer than redistributing).
#
# Anchored to the corpus rather than a repo-wide `*.pdf`. The unanchored form also
# swallowed spike/mex_rsa.pdf -- the ground-truth fixture pipeline/tests/conftest.py
# depends on -- so a fresh clone silently skipped those tests instead of running them.
# The spike report is STILL excluded, deliberately and for the same copyright reason
# (see the AR-16 note in conftest.py); it is now excluded by a line that says so.
pmsr-corpus/*.pdf
pmsr-corpus/*.part
pmsr-corpus/failures.txt
spike/*.pdf

# Profile-emission scratch directories (Story 1.18). `emit_profiles` stages both artifact
# namespaces into siblings and swaps them, retaining the retired copy until BOTH swaps land,
# so the 1,296 artifacts move all-or-nothing. A successful run removes these; a run killed
# mid-write cannot. They sit inside the COMMITTED data/index/ tree, so without this a
# sweeping `git add` after an aborted run would commit hundreds of orphan artifacts as
# though they were real -- and `identity.check_committed_data` would then pin them as the
# AD-3 immutability baseline, which is expensive to undo.
data/index/*.staged/
data/index/*.previous.rollback/

# The same scratch paths for the two write paths Story 1.19 made all-or-nothing, and the
# SHAPE differs because `pipeline/precompute/swap.py` puts scratch beside the target, not
# inside it. `emit_bundles` swaps `data/matches/` itself, so its siblings sit at the
# `data/` level -- `data/matches/*.staged/` would match nothing. `emit_index` swaps the two
# index artifacts as FILES (it must not touch the profile subdirectories), so its scratch
# paths are `data/index/tournament.json.staged` and friends: files, not directories, which
# the two directory-only patterns above cannot match either.
#
# Same failure mode as the block above, and it is not hypothetical: a run killed mid-write
# cannot clean up after itself, and without these a sweeping `git add` would commit the
# orphans as though they were real -- then `identity.check_committed_data` would pin them
# as the AD-3 immutability baseline, which is expensive to undo.
data/matches.staged/
data/matches.previous.rollback/
data/index/*.json.staged
data/index/*.json.previous.rollback

# `write_canonical`'s own temp, added by the 2026-08-07 code review of Story 1.19. It names
# temps `<name>.<pid>.tmp` (pipeline/ingest/records.py) and unlinks them itself on any
# exception -- but a HARD kill cannot, and the patterns above do not match a name ending
# `.tmp`. Bundle temps were already covered, because `data/matches.staged/` is ignored as a
# DIRECTORY and the temps live inside it; the index staging siblings are files at the
# `data/index/` level, so `data/index/tournament.json.staged.1234.tmp` was the one shape
# nothing matched. Pre-existing in kind -- the identical exposure existed for direct
# `tournament.json` writes before the staging siblings were introduced -- but the block above
# claims every scratch path is ignored, so it should be true.
data/index/*.tmp
